=== the one class the table calls HOST-EXPLAINED writes its event, and channel says which it is
=== a class that reaches a person cannot be recorded silently, whatever the caller believes
  asking -> exit 1
  question -> exit 1
  merge-failed -> exit 1
  dispatch-failed -> exit 1
  main-broken -> exit 1
  unfinished-twice -> exit 1

=== gap is a notification and this writer takes escalations, so it is refused here on the first
=== guard rather than on the disposition. The honest reason is the one shown, not swallowed.
  gap -> exit 1

=== the notification half. record_notification is the same act on the other channel, and its
=== guard is the one that has to work hardest: gap is not HOST-EXPLAINED by its class, it is
=== HOST-EXPLAINED for an event whose own evidence explains it — so this writer admits and
=== refuses the same class, on the fields and nothing else.
=== and every other reading of the same gap, each of which a person is owed
  host {"assessed":"unexplained","sleep_seconds":0} -> exit 1
  host {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"history-unreadable"} -> exit 1
  host null -> exit 1
=== a notification class that is never HOST-EXPLAINED, whatever is attached to it
  stall -> exit 1
  rate_limit -> exit 1
  takeover-silent -> exit 1
=== and the two refusals this writer inherits from the pair above: a class outside the list, and
=== a carries that is not JSON
  baton-unhealthy -> exit 1
  carries not json -> exit 1

=== the refusals a person reads, on the stream they belong to

=== the refusals the notification writer prints, on the stream they belong to

=== what was written: two lines, one per channel that is not a channel, and the notifier was
=== not called at all — calls.log is empty
{"kind":"escalation","class":"baton-unhealthy","scope":"project","key":null,"channel":["record"]}
{"kind":"notification","class":"gap","scope":null,"key":"2026-09-12T10:00:00+01:00","channel":["record"]}
{"kind":"escalation","class":"baton-unhealthy","scope":"project","key":null,"channel":["record"]}
{"kind":"notification","class":"gap","scope":null,"key":"2026-09-12T10:00:00+01:00","channel":["record"]}
